  "negation_guards": {
    "note": "If a trigger appears inside one of these constructions the hit is downgraded to 'weak' (still surfaced, but does not alone satisfy min_hits).",
    "patterns": [
      "i am not (?:saying|claiming|accusing)",
      "this is not (?:a )?(?:fraud|dispute)",
      "no one (?:misled|lied)",
      "i'm not going to (?:sue|complain to)",
      "i don't think (?:it was|this is) unauthorized",
      "unlike last time"
    ]
  },
  "document_scope_guards": {
    "note": "A local 90-character negation window is not enough when the customer opens with an explicit disclaimer and then describes the same vocabulary later: 'I am not saying this was unauthorized... it made me think we had been charged twice' tripped Reg E on the second clause and then the Reg E ownership rule misrouted the whole case. These patterns downgrade the named category across the WHOLE complaint. Scoped to specific categories on purpose \u2014 a disclaimer about a disputed charge says nothing about a fee practice.",
    "guards": [
      {
        "pattern": "i (?:want to be clear that i )?am not (?:saying|claiming|alleging)[^.]{0,60}unauthorized",
        "downgrades": [
          "REG_E_EFT"
        ]
      },
      {
        "pattern": "(?:this|it) is not (?:a )?(?:dispute|fraud|unauthorized)",
        "downgrades": [
          "REG_E_EFT"
        ]
      },
      {
        "pattern": "i (?:do not|don't) think (?:it was|this is|this was) (?:unauthorized|fraud)",
        "downgrades": [
          "REG_E_EFT"
        ]
      },
      {
        "pattern": "(?:the app|your app|the website) is wrong,? not the charge",
        "downgrades": [
          "REG_E_EFT"
        ]
      },
      {
        "pattern": "i (?:am|'m) not (?:going to )?(?:sue|suing|taking legal)",
        "downgrades": [
          "LEGAL_MEDIA_THREAT"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "tuning_disclosure": "Triggers marked in git history as added on 2026-10-08 were added after inspecting misses on our own synthetic corpus. Recall measured on that same corpus is therefore partly in-sample and optimistic. The 'quiet' complaints \u2014 genuinely regulatory, no trigger vocabulary \u2014 were deliberately NOT tuned for, and the recall figure on them is the honest indicator of this engine's ceiling."
